# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# Windows ends a line with CR+LF, macOS and Linux with LF alone. Without a rule
# here, a file committed from Windows carries its CRLF into the repo, and the
# first friend who opens it on a Mac sees every line of every file marked as
# changed. Their editor then "fixes" it back, and the two of you trade the same
# 159,000-line diff forever.
#
# "text=auto eol=lf" says: work out which files are text, store LF in the repo,
# and check out whatever the local machine prefers. Nobody has to think about it
# again, which is the point.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary files. Git already guesses these correctly, but the guess is a
# heuristic and the rule above is not. Saying it outright means no future
# pattern can ever line-ending-mangle a recording.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.opus binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
